Luck and religious activities are inter-related by: 
  Anger of the gods toward you,
  Alignment of you with your god,
  the between prayer time-out which is typically a minimum of 300
  moves and can be much longer.
		
Luck and Luckstones

  Your luck begins at 0, (+ or -1 depending on the moon), and can
range from -10 to +10. When modified, it will decrease or increase
(time-out) by 1 toward its starting value every 600 moves (300 for
angry gods), unless you're carrying a luckstone:
blessed   => good (positive) luck will not decrease,
uncursed  => good and bad luck will not time-out,
cursed    => bad (negative) luck will not increase.
While carrying a luckstone you may still change your luck.

Increasing Your Luck

* Throwing a gem at a unicorn:
    +5 (identified jewel & co-aligned unicorn)

    +1 (unidentified jewel)

    -3 to +3 (identified jewel & non-co-aligned unicorn)

* Sacrifice on a co-aligned altar:
    +0 to +5 (monster difficulty factor & sacrifice accepted & favor awarded)
    Seeing a four-leaf clover is a sign that your luck has improved.

    =0 (negative luck & not angry god)

    +1 (negative luck & angry god)

* Sacrifice on a non-co-aligned altar:
    +1 (negative luck & not angry god & successful)
        success = 25%, experience level 1 and increases such that
        success = 100% for experience level 6.

* Sacrificing a human corpse at a chaotic altar.
    +2 (chaotic only) 

* Sitting on a throne:
    +1 (negative luck, sometimes)

* Prayer:
    =0 (negative luck & not angry god, small chance)

Decreasing Your Luck

* Killing a co-aligned unicorn:
    -5

* Sacrificing a human:
    -5 (non-chaotic only)

* After converting to a new god, trying to sacrifice at the altar
  of your original god. conversion is accomplished by sacrificing
  at a non-co-aligned altar while your god is angry.
    -5

* Converting to a new god:
    -3

* Praying before your between prayer time-out expires:
    -3
 
* Breaking a mirror:
    -2

* Killing a friendly human:
    -2

* Killing a pet (tame monster):
    -1

* Desecrating (kicking or digging) a co-aligned altar:
    -1

* Killing a peaceful monster:
    -1 (50% chance)

* Sacrifice at a non-co-aligned altar:
    -1 (not angry god & failure)
        failure = 75% at experience level 1 and decreases such that
        failure = 0% at experience level 6.

* Hitting a blind monster:
    -1 (0.2% chance)

Your luck remains unchanged when you convert an altar or pray
successfully, except as noted above. Your gods may become angry
when you pray inappropriately.

